  "solution": {
    "text": "Tishchenko reaction is a modification of Canizzaro's reaction. This reaction involves disproportionation of an aldehyde lacking a hydrogen atom in the alpha position in the presence of an alkoxide. The reaction product is an ester. Catalysts are aluminium alkoxide or sodium alkoxide.\nIn Cannizzaro's reaction the base is sodium hydroxide and the oxidation product is a carboxylic acid and the reduction product is an alcohol.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/pfqfJzKmz8TigeXzLFw7HIfjVnG79BFQqVLQJgqBTO8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
